Input ports' state from one frame to the next in save states, so that a machine that loads a
state goes on exactly as the one that saved it (found with Cruis'n USA, the first game here with
analog controls the bar moves with keys; patches/0007).

MAME's input ports carry state across frames that its save states left out:

- analog_field: the accumulated position (m_accum), the previous one (m_previous, for mid-frame
  interpolation), the last raw analog value (m_previousanalog: an absolute device only moves the
  control when its value changes) and whether the last move was digital (m_lastdigital, which
  autocentring needs). Keys move a wheel or a pedal a little each frame and it goes back by itself
  when they let go, so a machine that loaded a state taken mid-turn started from its own wheel
  position: a watcher's Cruis'n USA, started from the player's state while they steered, drove
  another race from there. Time Crisis II's light gun position is one too.
- ioport_field_live: a digital field's last state (switch-down detection for impulse and toggle
  fields), its impulse count and a toggle's value.
- dynamic_field: the last value a field's change callback (PORT_CHANGED_MEMBER: Cruis'n USA's
  Shift Up/Down) or read callback saw. A machine that loaded a state taken with a shift button
  held saw a fresh press on its first frame, and shifted.

All registered once the ports' live state exists (ioport_manager::initialize), as items of the
"ioport_analog", "ioport_field", "ioport_write" and "ioport_read" modules by port tag and index.
This is MAME's core: every game's states grow by a few bytes per input field (Cruis'n USA by 395,
Tekken 3 by 198, Time Crisis II by 332).

diff --git a/src/emu/ioport.cpp b/src/emu/ioport.cpp
index 68248081..23d20a95 100644
--- a/src/emu/ioport.cpp
+++ b/src/emu/ioport.cpp
@@ -1848,6 +1848,7 @@ time_t ioport_manager::initialize()
 	// allocate live structures to mirror the configuration
 	for (auto &port : m_portlist)
 		port.second->init_live_state();
+	save_live_state();
 
 	// handle autoselection of devices
 	init_autoselect_devices({ IPT_AD_STICK_X,  IPT_AD_STICK_Y,   IPT_AD_STICK_Z }, OPTION_ADSTICK_DEVICE,    "analog joystick");
@@ -1872,6 +1873,54 @@ time_t ioport_manager::initialize()
 }
 
 
+//-------------------------------------------------
+//  save_live_state - what the inputs carry from
+//  one frame to the next goes in save states
+//  (the arcade bar: a machine that loads a state
+//  must go on exactly as the one that saved it)
+//-------------------------------------------------
+
+void ioport_manager::save_live_state()
+{
+	for (auto &port : m_portlist)
+	{
+		const char *const tag = port.second->tag();
+		ioport_port_live &live = port.second->live();
+
+		// an analog control's position: keys move a wheel or a pedal a little each frame, and
+		// it goes back by itself (Cruis'n USA); a light gun's last position (Time Crisis II)
+		int index = 0;
+		for (analog_field &analog : live.analoglist)
+		{
+			machine().save().save_item(nullptr, "ioport_analog", tag, index, analog.m_accum, "accum");
+			machine().save().save_item(nullptr, "ioport_analog", tag, index, analog.m_previous, "previous");
+			machine().save().save_item(nullptr, "ioport_analog", tag, index, analog.m_previousanalog, "previousanalog");
+			machine().save().save_item(nullptr, "ioport_analog", tag, index, analog.m_lastdigital, "lastdigital");
+			index++;
+		}
+
+		// a digital field's state last frame (its impulse count, a toggle's value)
+		index = 0;
+		for (ioport_field &field : port.second->fields())
+		{
+			machine().save().save_item(nullptr, "ioport_field", tag, index, field.live().value, "value");
+			machine().save().save_item(nullptr, "ioport_field", tag, index, field.live().impulse, "impulse");
+			machine().save().save_item(nullptr, "ioport_field", tag, index, field.live().last, "last");
+			index++;
+		}
+
+		// the last value a field's change callback saw (Cruis'n USA's shift buttons), or its
+		// read callback gave
+		index = 0;
+		for (dynamic_field &dynfield : live.writelist)
+			machine().save().save_item(nullptr, "ioport_write", tag, index++, dynfield.m_oldval, "oldval");
+		index = 0;
+		for (dynamic_field &dynfield : live.readlist)
+			machine().save().save_item(nullptr, "ioport_read", tag, index++, dynfield.m_oldval, "oldval");
+	}
+}
+
+
